        content:
          "The reading comprehension section (Leestueck / Comprension de Lectura) is worth a significant portion of the exam. You are given texts in Spanish and must answer questions, usually in Spanish.\n\n" +
          "STEP-BY-STEP STRATEGY:\n" +
          "1. READ THE QUESTIONS FIRST - Before reading the text, skim all the questions. This tells you what to look for and focuses your reading. Underline key words in the questions.\n\n" +
          "2. READ THE TITLE AND INTRODUCTION - These give you the topic and context. A title like 'Los jovenes y la tecnologia' immediately tells you the theme.\n\n" +
          "3. FIRST READING - Read the entire text quickly for general understanding (gist). Don't panic about unknown words. Try to understand the overall topic and main ideas of each paragraph.\n\n" +
          "4. SECOND READING - Read more carefully, matching paragraphs to questions. Most comprehension questions follow the order of the text - Q1 relates to the beginning, Q2 to the middle, etc.\n\n" +
          "5. ANSWER IN SPANISH - Unless told otherwise, answer in Spanish. Use your own words where possible, but you CAN lift relevant phrases from the text. Do not copy entire sentences if the question asks you to explain.\n\n" +
          "6. CHECK YOUR ANSWERS - Make sure you've answered what was asked. If the question asks 'por que' (why), your answer needs a reason. If it asks 'como' (how), explain the method/manner.\n\n" +
          "COMMON QUESTION TYPES:\n" +
          "- Segun el texto... (According to the text...) = find the specific information\n" +
          "- Que opina el autor sobre...? (What does the author think about...?) = identify opinion\n" +
          "- Que significa la palabra X en el contexto? (What does word X mean in context?)\n" +
          "- Verdadero o falso? (True or false?) = always justify your answer\n" +
          "- Resume con tus propias palabras... (Summarise in your own words...)\n" +
          "- Pon un titulo al texto (Give the text a title) = summarise the main theme",
