        "title": "General Listening Approach",
        "content": "The Listening Comprehension (Cluastuiscint) is worth 100 marks and lasts approximately 40 minutes at Higher Level. You will hear each recording twice, with a pause between playings. Use the first listening to get the gist and identify the topic, speakers, and tone. Use the second listening to confirm your answers and fill in specific details you missed. Always read ALL questions before the recording begins so you know what information to listen for. Write your answers in English unless the question specifically asks for Spanish. Keep answers concise and factual - you do not earn extra marks for long answers, and a wrong detail added to a correct answer can lose you marks. Pay close attention to numbers, dates, times, and proper nouns, as these are frequently tested. If you hear a word you do not recognise, try to guess from context or from similar words you know. Negative constructions (no, nunca, ni...ni, tampoco) can reverse the meaning of an entire sentence, so listen for them carefully. Be aware that speakers may use colloquial expressions or speak at a natural pace with connected speech, elision, and regional accents. Time management is critical: if you miss an answer on the first play, leave it and move on rather than losing focus on subsequent questions. Write something for every question, as a blank answer scores zero but an educated guess might earn partial marks. After the second listening, use any remaining time to review your answers for logic and completeness.",
